{"content":"---\nname: collatz-h23a-bridge\ndescription: \"Map of the prior Collatz project's H23a work and its bridges to the finite-spectral-shadows program\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: 3d506146-0c9f-463a-a710-cacb38cea0a3\n---\n\nThe \"other side\" of H23a lives in the original Collatz project at `/home/john/mynotes/collatz/` (Lean: `lean4/`; docs: `docs/`). Key files and bridges to the current program ([[project-defect-cocycle-csuite]], `deterministic_equidistribution_theory/finite_spectral_shadows.tex`):\n\n- **`docs/h23a_hardening_findings.md`** + **`docs/stabilized_residue_extinction.tex`** (SRCE, 32pp, Appendix A) — H23a at MIXED moduli Q=2^r3^s with the explicit per-Q certificate (C_Q, Γ_Q, α_Q, Δ_Q, η_Q=α_Q(1−cosΔ_Q), M_Q, L_0(Q)), computed by `c_scripts/cert_full.c` for 25 moduli; H1–H4 module structure (cocycle perturbation, stabilisation, Wielandt accessibility, non-coboundary gap). Their \"no nontrivial character is a coboundary at any grid Q\" was numerical — the new program's Cob=⟨χ₂⟩ classification theorem is its structural completion (note: their additive 2-adic chars at high r approach coboundary, Δ_Q→0 — consistent with the parity/χ₂ direction housing the unique coboundary). Remaining there: finite-dimensional H1–H2 perturbation bookkeeping. **This is the complementary FINITE-Q certificate route if the asymptotic (lift-phase) route stalls.**\n- **`docs/why_collatz_fails.md`** — the postmortem: the wall = quenched equidistribution/deterministic normality of the valuation cocycle (= our keystone, verbatim); three theories fail structurally (dynamical Borel–Cantelli needs a.e.; ×2,×3 rigidity fails because the cocycle is ×3-rank-one (pvt_14/15); no homogeneous encoding); Tao 2022 = annealed frontier. Lean names the obstruction: open sorry `equidistribution_implies_deficit_bounded`.\n- **`docs/pvt_17_realizability_findings.md`** (+ pvt_3..22 series) — realizability (wish-list #8): actual orbits vs confined renewal controls are WORD-LEVEL INDISTINGUISHABLE (restart density, mean b, A_m/3^m all match); the SOLE gap is **canonical-residue pinning**: actual log₂(r_w)/D_m → 0 vs 0.99 for synthetic. Bridges directly to the window variable X_w / lift-phase structure of the new program.\n- **`docs/sparse_target_inverse_theorem.tex`** — their keystone-shaped inverse theorem; **`docs/pointwise_valuation.tex`** (PVT); **`docs/master_dependencies.tex`** — the four open inputs tracker; **`docs/knowledge_graph.md`**.\n- Lean4 formalization at `lean4/` (sorry inventory in `docs/lean4_formalization.org`).\n\nConvention caution: their κ_Q ≥ 0.99 is a differently-normalized directly-measured residue gap at mixed moduli (additive characters) — not comparable to the new program's γ_c/κ_Q at pure 3^c multiplicative sectors.\n","filePath":"/home/john/.claude/projects/-home-john-mynotes/memory/collatz_h23a_bridge.md","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[],"type":"create","userModified":false}